hello and welcome to modeling the  masters a new series dedicated to  helping entrepreneurs find a shortcut to  business success by modeling the  strategies and ideas of other famous  successful entrepreneurs you can learn  viable strategies to implement into your  business today to achieve success for  your company modeling the Masters and  their strategy is quite simply as the  fastest way to go from credit card debt  to business success my name is Evan  Carmichael and today we're gonna be  talking about the Harley Davidson Motor  Company  hey what may be an American icon today  when it was first started was founded by  two young entrepreneurs with an idea a  big dream and the willingness to make it  happen  we're gonna learn a little bit about  their story how they got started what  factors led to their success and what  take-home lessons you can implement your  business today to achieve success on  your own the first lesson from Harley  Davidson is build a great team it's  extremely difficult to build a great  company as a one-person operation which  a lot of entrepreneurs unfortunately are  when Harley Davidson started it was  started by two young entrepreneurs  William Harley and Arthur Davidson when  they were 20 and 21 years old  they started the business unfortunately  didn't know a lot about actually  building motorcycles they took bicycles  tried to put an engine on top of it and  it wasn't working out for them they  needed somebody with a little bit more  experience so they brought in Walter  Davidson was an older brother from  Kansas they promised him a chance to  ride on the motorcycle he only later  found out that he had to actually build  the cycle for them but he stayed on  later on as a company grew they also  brought in William  to be the first official president of  the organization so it's important to  really surround yourself with the people  who can help your business get to that  next step  realize what you're really good at and  find people who are really good at the  other areas and you don't want to touch  it or that you can't be bothered with or  you're not really gonna be passionate  about if you focus on your core  strengths like the harley-davidson team  did everybody focuses in on what they're  really good at then you have a much  greater chance of achieving success  lesson number two is build slowly when  the company was first started and they  made their first motorcycles in 1903  they only made three the next year they  made another three the next year they  made only seven more and finally the  next year they expand it and were able  to make 50 when they started there were  no employees it was just the founders  they were working on sweat equity alone  they didn't spend the money to go and  get warm ploys and dig themselves into  debt and when they started their first  center of operation was a little shed  they had built in their backyard and  their sister Hannah wrote Harley  Davidson Motor Company on the outside of  the door it wasn't until their fourth  year that they were able to expand to a  full level Factory and build those 50  motorcycles too many entrepreneurs when  they get started take on too much debt  they borrow money from all sorts of  different sources and then they blow  their brains out trying to accomplish  rapid growth don't overextend yourself  build slowly make sure that you have a  product that people are willing to pay  money for and then be able to build your  company and grow through the profits  being reinvested into your  lesson number three is sell to big  companies one of the major reasons for  the success of harley-davidson was their  ability to secure the big contract some  of the big deals at the Atlanta tour  with the United States Postal Service  the police departments and the allies  during World War one and World War two  it's a lot easier to find a big company  and sell them a thousand copies of units  of whatever you're selling to try to go  out and sell thousand different people  one copy or one unit of whatever you're  selling go out and try to find those big  customers when the recession hit the  Great Depression in the United States  and around the world before that hit  there were 300 different manufacturers  of motorcycles in the United States  after a hit they were - and the main  reason why they only get through it so  well was their ability to keep with  those big contracts find the big  contracts and one or two major cuts of  customers keep them happy and look you  coming back for more lesson number four  is leverage big brands one of the best  marketing decisions that harley-davidson  ever made was to sponsor a team of  racers called the wrecking crew these  were guys who went out and raced  motorcycles they won all the races and  they were known for their dangerous  stunts in their style by being able to  associate with this group they passed on  a lot of brand value to harley-davidson  suddenly everybody knew who  harley-davidson was it's not unlike what  Nike does now by sponsoring some of the  top athletes so for your own business  think about who you can partner up with  who was already a known entity people  know about them they have a respected  brand and by latching onto them  partnering with them you've gained  instant credibility it's hard to go from  nothing people don't know who you are to  becoming that rising star and an easy  way to do it is by leveraging the brand  that others have already built  harley-davidson continued to do this as  they grew their company when they  partnered with the police departments  and with the Allies during World War one  in World War two because people look up  to the police and to the Allies when  they saw that the police and allies were  using Harley Davidsons then they must be  a good product and everybody else wanted  to get them as well so think about who  you can leverage a brand that's in your  industry or related to your industry you  tagged on to them and they can help take  you to that next level of success our  final lesson lesson number five is  innovate Harley Davidson was always on  the cutting edge of innovation for their  motorcycles and they were known for  always having high quality new  technologies coming through to make  their motorcycles more reliable and  faster they were the first ones to have  the step starter so you didn't have to  ride the bike for a certain amount of  time before the engine would kick in  they would first is the v-twin engine  and they were the first ones that break  all sorts of different land speed  records with their motorcycles  especially in tough economic times it's  important to invest in your research and  development and have the best product  possible if your product is similar to  everybody else's and the price is the  same as everybody else's it's going to  be hard to stand out give customers a  reason to buy from you by making a  product as good as it possibie invest in  making it the best technology out there  on the market so the customers have no  choice but to buy from you today  harley-davidson has almost 10,000  employees and almost 6 billion dollars  in revenue it seems like a really big  company now but remember when it first  got started it was two young  entrepreneurs with an idea a big dream  willingness to make it happen and by  following those five lessons that we  talked about today you can also achieve  success and build a great company for  you  I hope you enjoyed the session today I  wanted to thank phantom media or the  sponsors of this event you can learn  more about them by clicking on the links  provided and as well you can learn more  about Riley Davidson on their stories  and the stories of other famous  entrepreneurs on our website at  economical calm I hope you enjoyed the  session and look forward to the next  modeling the master series with you
 

